AN7581: complete the OEM spi.ko transaction layer in en75xx_zsi (006).

Follow-up to 005 (build-9/11: the static interface-mode write and the
SLIC0 reset pulse moved the signature from 0x00 to 0xff, but the
Le9642/43 still never answers).  Capstone disassembly of the stock
spi.ko (ZSI_bytes_write @0x3400, ZSI_bytes_read @0x32c0, SPI_cfg @0x2e0,
SPI_Reset @0x1f50; report:
devices/ZN504XG-D/reports/a1_spi_ko_diff_report_20261021.md) shows the
OEM driver does three more things our driver never did:

  - Writes the wrapper chip-select register (PA 0x1fbd1014 = cs) before
    EVERY ZSI transaction on HIR 0xE/0xC.  Our driver has no 0x14 write
    at all; with no chip selected the transaction lands nowhere and the
    bus floats high - the exact 0xff ff signature observed on the 504.
  - Pokes the wrapper control register (0x00) before every transaction:
    (v & 0xe0ffffef) | 0xf0000010.  Idempotent; converges to
    0xf0030313, i.e. the OEM steady-state top byte is 0xf0 whereas the
    init value programmed once is 0x0f030313.
  - SPI_Reset runs the interface mode as a reset dance (0x1fb00094 low
    nibble 0 -> f -> 5 with delays) and pulses 0x1fb00834 bit 4 around
    the SLIC0 pulse on HIR 0xC/0xE, instead of a single static write.

Changes (all in en75xx_zsi.c, non-legacy AN7581 path only):

  - New wrapper register defines ZSI_CS_SEL (0x14) and the per-tx poke
    masks ZSI_TX_PREP_KEEP / ZSI_TX_PREP_SET.
  - zsi_prep_transaction_locked(): CS write + control-reg poke, called
    under the tx mutex from en75xx_zsi_write/read_reg/write_reg.
  - en75xx_zsi_slic_reset(): OEM mode dance before the SLIC0 pulse and
    a SYS_RESET bit4 pulse after it, with OEM delay values.
  - Three module params defaulting to OEM behaviour for blind A/B from
    /etc/modules.d: zsi_cs (0x14 value, 0xff = never write),
    tx_prep, reset_mode_dance.  DT property airoha,zsi-cs overrides
    zsi_cs.
  - Probe banner prints cs/tx_prep/mode_dance so the debug build proves
    which path ran.

Acceptance (build-13, same byte-level gate as build-11): dmesg shows
"Le964%c detected (rcn 08 pcn ..)" instead of "unexpected chip id ff ff",
and the FXS character device appears.

Signed-off-by: ZN504XG-D voice porting project
